From 5daa7952b5e466c954be52a9838726212c0337ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Khaled <khaledchoucri@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:33:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] POC-10a: shared chip folder, chip pack, can-learn chips,
 copies as stamina, type candy

One folder for the party (30 + 2 per extra Pokemon), auto-built from the chip
pack. A chip is a move: whoever is in battle uses it if its species can learn
it (generated can-learn table). No PP: copies are the stamina; folders under 15
chips still reshuffle. Learning a move grants one copy (first code). Dead chips
leave the hand. Catching gives type candy (catch-rate based, x3 first catch).
pkbn.sav v2 (v1 migrates).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01FbWSqvcg6G5Gpw6ynvR5tJ
---
